From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000081 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@local>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mips: sf2000: split copied init prologue probe

The direct-syscall-probe image stops at marker 0x51510009, before the copied
/init prologue reaches marker 0x5151000a. Split the replayed prologue into
smaller retained checkpoints so the next hardware run identifies whether the
stack adjustment, argument setup, or first stack stores are failing.

Move the direct syscall probe farther down the stub page to leave room for the
expanded entry probe. The final path is unchanged: after the split prologue
reaches marker 0x5151000a, it records 0x5151000e and jumps directly to the
syscall probe.
---
 fs/binfmt_elf.c | 93 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------------
 1 file changed, 70 insertions(+), 23 deletions(-)

--- a/fs/binfmt_elf.c
+++ b/fs/binfmt_elf.c
@@ -227,10 +227,9 @@ static void sf2000_elf_copy_identity_stub(unsigned long entry,
 	unsigned long probe = CKSEG0ADDR(SF2000_IDENTITY_STUB_ADDR +
 		96 * sizeof(u32));
 	unsigned long syscall_probe = CKSEG0ADDR(SF2000_IDENTITY_STUB_ADDR +
-		160 * sizeof(u32));
+		256 * sizeof(u32));
 	unsigned long trampoline = CKSEG0ADDR(SF2000_IDENTITY_STUB_ADDR +
 		64 * sizeof(u32));
-	unsigned int i;
 
 	if (!IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_MIPS_SF2000))
 		return;
